Description: Keep each VP2 H.264 reference in its place in the reference tables
 The motion vectors PBSP stores with a picture name its references by
 their place in the BSP and VP reference tables, and temporal direct
 prediction in B pictures reads the co-located picture's vectors. The
 tables were filled in the order the application lists the references,
 which FFmpeg changes at every picture, so B pictures predicted with
 temporal direct came out wrong. A reference now keeps its place in both
 tables while it is one, and new ones take free places.
